# PRD: On-Page & Off-Page SEO Module

**Product:** SEO Audit SaaS (Crawler + Dashboard)
**Feature:** On-Page SEO Analysis + Off-Page SEO (Backlink) Analysis
**Author:** Noor Fatima
**Status:** Draft
**Version:** 1.0

---

## 1. Overview

The core crawler currently audits performance (Core Web Vitals) and generates auto-fix recommendations. This module extends the crawler's existing per-page audit pass to also evaluate **on-page SEO factors** (things fully controlled by the site owner: titles, headings, content, internal links) and adds a new **off-page SEO layer** (things outside the site owner's direct control: backlinks, domain authority, referring domains) sourced from a third-party backlink API.

Together, these two additions turn the tool from a "technical + performance auditor" into a **complete SEO health auditor** — matching the core value proposition of competitors like eRank/Marmalead-style tools but for general websites rather than Etsy specifically (relevant since this is separate from your Etsy-focused RankForge project).

---

## 2. Problem Statement

Right now the audit gives a performance score and generic recommendations, but it doesn't answer the two questions every client actually asks:

1. "Is my content and page structure actually optimized for the keywords I want to rank for?" → **On-page gap**
2. "Why isn't my site ranking even though the page itself looks fine?" → **Off-page gap** (this is almost always a backlink/authority problem, which nothing in the current tool detects)

Without these, the audit is incomplete — a client can have a perfect Core Web Vitals score and still not rank, and the tool currently has no way to explain why.

---

## 3. Goals

- Add automated on-page SEO scoring using data already available from the existing crawl (no new crawl pass needed — extend the current page-parsing step).
- Add off-page SEO scoring via a third-party backlink API integration.
- Surface both as new sections in the existing audit report (dashboard + PDF) using the same score-card visual pattern already established (SEO Health, Performance, Mobile, Schema).
- Feed on-page issues into the existing `RecommendationEngine` so they show up as actionable, severity-ranked items — not just a separate silo.
- Keep off-page API costs controlled via caching, since this is the most expensive part of the audit per site.

## 4. Non-Goals (v1)

- Real-time backlink monitoring / alerts (future phase)
- Full competitor SEO audit (only backlink gap comparison is in scope, not full competitor page audits)
- Historical trend charts for on-page/off-page scores (v1 stores the data; trend visualization is a v2 addition once 2+ audits exist per site)
- Keyword rank tracking (SERP position monitoring) — separate future module
- Automated on-page fixes via API (e.g., auto-editing title tags) — this exists for a narrower set of items in the existing WordPress REST API auto-fix flow; on-page SEO items beyond that (content length, internal linking) are recommendation-only in v1, not auto-fixed

---

## 5. Users & Use Cases

**Primary user:** You / your agency clients (site owners, small business owners who hired the audit).
**Secondary user:** SEO freelancers/agencies white-labeling the tool for their own clients.

**Key use case:** A client's site has good technical health but isn't ranking. The audit needs to immediately surface "your DA is 12 and you have 3 referring domains — that's why" alongside "your homepage H1 is missing and your blog posts average 180 words — that's thin content." This diagnostic clarity is the core deliverable.

