## 6. Functional Requirements

### 6.1 On-Page SEO Checks

| # | Check | Data Source | Pass/Fail Logic |
|---|-------|-------------|------------------|
| 1 | Title tag | Existing crawl HTML | Exists, 50–60 chars, contains target keyword if provided |
| 2 | Meta description | Existing crawl HTML | Exists, 150–160 chars, not duplicated across pages |
| 3 | Heading structure | Existing crawl HTML | Exactly one H1; logical H2/H3 nesting (no skipped levels) |
| 4 | Content length | Existing crawl HTML | Flag if <300 words ("thin content") |
| 5 | Keyword density | Existing crawl HTML + target keyword input | 0.5%–2.5% healthy range |
| 6 | Readability | Existing crawl HTML | Flesch Reading Ease score via `textstat` |
| 7 | URL structure | Page URL | <75 chars, hyphens not underscores, no uppercase |
| 8 | Internal linking | Existing crawl (all page URLs known from sitemap) | Flag orphan pages (0 inbound internal links), broken internal links |
| 9 | Canonical tag | Existing crawl HTML | Exists, self-referencing (or intentionally points elsewhere) |
| 10 | Image alt text | Existing crawl HTML | Already partially built — extend to full-site % coverage score |

**Requirement:** All 10 checks run during the existing crawl pass (no additional HTTP requests). Each check outputs `{status, issue, severity}` consistent with the existing `RecommendationEngine` input shape so results merge into the same recommendations list.

### 6.2 Off-Page SEO Checks

| # | Check | Data Source | Notes |
|---|-------|-------------|-------|
| 1 | Domain Authority (DA) | Backlink API (Moz/SEMrush) | Cached, refreshed weekly per site |
| 2 | Page Authority (PA) | Backlink API | Per top-level pages, not every page (cost control) |
| 3 | Total backlinks | Backlink API | |
| 4 | Referring domains | Backlink API | More important than raw backlink count |
| 5 | Spam score | Backlink API | Flag if >30% |
| 6 | Anchor text distribution | Backlink API | Branded vs exact-match vs generic — over-optimized anchor text is a penalty risk |
| 7 | Competitor backlink gap | Backlink API, requires a competitor domain input from the user | Domains linking to competitor but not to client site |

**Requirement:** Off-page data is fetched **once per audit cycle** (not per page — this is domain-level, not page-level data) and cached for 7 days minimum to control API cost, since backlink profiles don't meaningfully change hour-to-hour.

**Requirement:** If no backlink API key is configured (e.g., free-tier user), the off-page section shows an upsell/locked state rather than breaking the audit — on-page results must still generate fully.

