## 7. Technical Requirements

### 7.1 Backend (Python Crawler)

- `OnPageAuditor` class extends the existing per-page audit — hooks into the same `BeautifulSoup` object already parsed during the crawl (no re-fetch).
- New dependency: `textstat` for readability scoring.
- `OffPageAuditor` class is a separate service, called once per full-site audit (not per page), with its own caching layer (Redis or a Supabase table with a `last_fetched` timestamp check before calling the API).
- Both new auditors output data in the same schema shape the `RecommendationEngine` already expects (`severity`, `category`, `issue`, `fixes`, `automatable`) so no changes are needed to the recommendation/PDF pipeline itself — only new input feeding into it.

### 7.2 Backend (Database — Supabase)

New columns/tables needed:
- `audits` table: add `onpage_score INT`, `offpage_score INT`
- New table `backlink_snapshots`: `website_id`, `domain_authority`, `page_authority`, `total_backlinks`, `referring_domains`, `spam_score`, `fetched_at` — this is the cache layer for off-page data
- New table `onpage_issues`: per-audit breakdown (can reuse existing `recommendations_log` table with `category = 'onpage'`)

### 7.3 Backend (API Choice for Off-Page)

- **v1 recommendation: Moz API** — cheapest entry point (~$99+/mo), sufficient DA/PA/backlink data for MVP.
- Ahrefs has superior data but pricing isn't built for reselling via a SaaS (enterprise-oriented) — revisit only if pricing model changes or at scale.
- SEMrush is a viable alternative if you're already using it for anything else in the stack.
- **Decision needed from you:** which provider to commit to before backend work starts, since the response schema differs per provider and `OffPageAuditor` will be written against one specific API.

### 7.4 Frontend (React Dashboard)

- New `OnPageSection` and `OffPageSection` components, following the same `ScoreCard`/`MetricCard` visual pattern already used for Performance and SEO Health.
- On-page issues merge into the existing `RecommendationsSection` (filterable list) rather than living in an entirely separate UI silo — so a client sees ONE prioritized list, not four disconnected tabs.
- Off-page section shows a locked/upsell state if no backlink API key is configured for that plan tier.

### 7.5 PDF Report

- `ReportGenerator` gets two new sections: On-Page Findings, Off-Page Findings — inserted between "Score Overview" and "Recommendations" in the existing PDF flow.

