## 8. Scoring Methodology

- **On-Page Score (0–100):** weighted average across the 10 checks in 6.1. Suggested initial weights: Title (15%), Meta Description (10%), Headings (15%), Content Length (15%), Keyword Density (10%), Readability (10%), URL (5%), Internal Linking (10%), Canonical (5%), Image Alt (5%). *(Adjust weights after testing on a few real sites — these are starting estimates, not final.)*
- **Off-Page Score (0–100):** primarily driven by normalized DA (0–100 already), adjusted down by spam score, adjusted up/down by referring domain growth trend once historical data exists (v2).

---

## 9. Success Metrics

- On-page audit adds **zero additional crawl time** (runs off existing page data) — measurable via crawl duration before/after.
- Off-page data fetch stays within **1 API call per site per week** (cache hit rate ≥ 85% on repeat audits within 7 days).
- Client-facing: % of audits where on-page or off-page issues are cited as the top severity issue (validates that these checks are actually catching things performance/schema checks were missing).

